# Curated source repository: never commit upstream checkouts or build state.
chromium_dev/
src/
chroot/
out/
depot_tools/
depot_tools_fresh/
chromite/
infra/
infra_virtualenv/
bazel_deps/
manifest/
.repo/

# Local build, package, cache, and deployment state.
package-staging/
private-repo/
private-repo.*
build-artifact-backups/
tmp-build-backups/
.ninja-tmpfs-backups/
.makepkg-*/
**/pkg/
**/src/
# auradefs is written in Rust, and Rust puts its source in src/. The rule
# above is aimed at the src/ and pkg/ directories makepkg creates beside a
# PKGBUILD, and it swallowed all fifty five .rs files in the daemon: not one
# of them has ever been tracked. The same thing happened to the wallpapers
# further down, for the same reason, and the fix is the same.
#
# vendor/ is not a cache. sevenz-rust2 is a path dependency carrying a local
# patch described in vendor/sevenz-rust2/AURADE-PATCH.md, so losing it loses
# a modification nothing can regenerate.
!auradefs/workspace/crates/*/src/
!auradefs/workspace/vendor/*/src/
# Cargo's build output, if a workspace build is ever run in place rather
# than through ci/build-auradefs-package.sh, which points CARGO_TARGET_DIR
# elsewhere. It is regenerable and large; the src/ negations above keep the
# real source tracked regardless.
auradefs/workspace/target/
auradefs/workspace/target-dev/
# makepkg's BUILDDIR when ci/build-private-repo.sh drives it.
.build/
deploy/
artifacts/
output/

# Logs, crash dumps, screenshots, and generated archives.
*.log
*.strace
*.core
core
*.dump
*.png
!assets/*.png
# Artwork cut from the logo by installer/tools/extract-brand-assets.py.
# Tracked so the image build and the tests can just read it, and kept
# honest by the theme test, which re-extracts and compares.
!installer/assets/*.png
# The wallpaper set. Tracked because it is a deliverable rather than a build
# artifact: nothing in this repository can regenerate these, and the only
# other copy was in a tmpfs. `*.png` above is aimed at screenshots and crash
# dumps, and it silently swallowed all twenty eight of them once.
!installer/wallpapers/*.png
# The boot screen's drawn assets. `installer/tools/make-plymouth-aurora.py`
# regenerates it and the theme test compares, so this is the same arrangement
# as the brand artwork above. Listed because `*.png` swallowed it too, exactly
# as it swallowed the wallpapers, and a silently untracked file in a theme
# directory is a boot screen that works here and is missing on the image.
!installer/archiso/airootfs/usr/share/plymouth/themes/aurade/*.png
