# Internal notes: keep them, never publish them.
#
# These were scrubbed from the public repository because they carry machine
# paths, VM addresses, build hosts, session transcripts and planning language.
# They are still wanted locally, so they are ignored rather than deleted: they
# can sit in the working tree beside the code they describe and cannot be
# committed by accident.
#
# Ignoring is not the protection, it is the convenience.
# `ci/public-release-leak-gate.sh` is the protection, because it refuses when
# one of these is tracked, and `git add -f` walks straight past a .gitignore.
.discord-bot-token
AURADE_*.md
ARCH_EXTRA_READINESS.md
DISCORD_MESSAGE_PACKET.md
REFERENCE.md
*_BACKLOG.md
*_HANDOFF.md
*_REVIEW.md
*_STATUS.md
*_STEPS.md
docs/handoff/
*handoff*.md
private-docs/

# A local, per-machine release wrapper that hardcodes a GNUPGHOME and signing
# paths for this build box. No key material, but it belongs to the machine, not
# the public repo, so it is kept out of any git add.
ci/.rc-signed.sh

# Local wallpaper authoring files. The catalog and images above are public;
# prompts and the generator stay on the build machine.
installer/wallpapers/.private/
